pread these  oats in a nice even layer covering most  of the apples put this in the microwave  for three to four minutes until the top  is golden brown and crispy all right  it's out of the microwave it's looking  awesome you can tell all those juices  thickened up just from that little bit  of flour and i cannot wait to dig in but  first  a little garnish some whipped cream  and lastly a little cinnamon i mean i  think this is so cute i actually think  it's really pretty it looks awesome  let's try it  the apples are tender they're full of  that cinnamon flavor and the crisp is so  crunchy honestly this is really good but  if you have a little bit more time and  you want to make pie for more than just  yourself let me show you how to make  this 60 minute apple pie  so what i love about this recipe is it's  more close to your traditional apple pie  but it is not going to take up your  whole day to make it so first thing  we're going to do is peel our apples  make sure you have a good peeler and  your work will go much quicker so we're  using two types of apples today we're  using golden delicious and gala apples  gala i don't know we're using those  because they're a softer type of apple  and they'll cook quicker in our pie and  save us time and then we're going to  slice them a little bit thinner than you  normally would  so in culinary school we had to practice  our knife cuts on potatoes and carrots  so i used to sneak potatoes in my bag  and take them home so i could practice  because i wanted to do the best  so that's all of our apples so now we're  just gonna add brown sugar lemon juice  so they don't brown corn starch to  thicken it cinnamon nutmeg  and salt you never bake without salt so  we're going to toss this all together  and we're going to let it sit while we  assemble our pie crust we have a  store-bought pie crust we're just going  to roll it out a little bit  wider than the width of our pan and  that's because we want to create those  really fun edges and we need a little  bit of length on the end to get that so  this is looking wide enough to me what  i'm gonna do is roll it up brushing off  any extra flour along the way  and then bring your pie pan to you  and gently roll it in  and magically it's in your pan press it  down on the bottom  so it reaches the edges brush off any  excess flour  okay so now we're going to add all of  those apples we're just going to put  this in the fridge while we make our top  crust so for my top crust i rolled it  out to about a 12 inch circle and what  i'm going to do is cut it in strips to  make a pretty lattice shape on top so it  kind of upgrades our pie so nobody has  to know that we use store-bought dough  so we have to make six one-inch strips  and eight half-inch strips  take your longest piece first and place  it in the middle and this is going to be  your guide so we'll lay two of the half  inch strips in between each of the  one-inch strips pull back each of the  one-inch strips and gently place another  one-inch strip horizontally across then  fold the one in strips back down over so  you're going to keep doing that process  alternating between the thick pieces and  the thin pieces until you get that  beautiful lattice design so now we're  going to do the edge we're going to do  something kind of different and roll it  inward tucking all those little bits in  so nobody has to see those jagged edges  we're going to start the crimping  process so use your knuckle to like dig  in and then use your thumb and index  finger to push back and just keep going  around  so now what we want to do is just brush  off any of that excess flour because  when we add the egg wash next we really  want that to stick to the crust and now  our last step is to add some raw sugar  on top just to give it another little  crunch so we're going to bake this in a  425 degree oven for 40 minutes covering  halfway through until the crust is  golden brown and the juices are bubbling  let's go  all right she's out of the oven she's  golden she's glossy from the egg white  i'm really excited to try it let's dig  in  i like don't want to cut her because  she's too pretty  um  for a 60 minute pie that came together  with just a little bit of effort the  filling has tons of cinnamon flavor the  crust is super crunchy and that raw  sugar just gives it that little bit of  edge but if you have more time and you  really want to impress your friends and  family stick with me for this next  recipe  now i'm going to show you how to make my  six hour salted caramel deep dish apple  pie so first what we're going to do is  just season our flour then we're going  to add in our cold butter i cut this in  about half inch cubes and i actually  popped it in the freezer for about 15  minutes just so it's really cold and  firm so what i like to do is like make  sure each of the pieces is coated in  flour before i start smashing them toss  it onto the next one also i find this  therapeutic like i can just zone out the  kids yelling at me i can just zone out  and just keep doing my dough okay so  that is looking awesome the next step is  to add ice water a tablespoon at a time  so i like to toss it up in the air like  this just to incorporate that water and  then add a little bit more so we're  using ice cold water because we don't  want to melt that butter and you know  that there's enough water in it when you  press together and it holds together so  now that this is shaggy looking i'm  going to transfer it on the table  and finish bringing it all together i'm  going to wrap them in plastic and just  pop them in the fridge for about an hour  to let the gluten relax while that's  happening we'll make our filling so for  this filling we're doing something a  little bit different this time we're  gonna par cook the apples before they go  in the oven to bake so to start we have  two tablespoons of unsalted butter  melting we have a big bowl of apples  i'm gonna add them right in  we 